   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">01 Jul 2020 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/adb-support-improved-connectivity-kiribatis-outer-islands</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">16 Dec 2021 | Article: https://www.adb.org/news/features/adb-world-bank-partnership-helping-pacific-reach-development-goals</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant 0713: 83% of contracts awarded and 42% disbursed as of 23 Apr 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: Recruitment of the individual consultants under the Outer Islands Implementation Unit (OIIU) is complete except for the Senior Engineer position, which may no longer be needed. Individual contracts under the OIIU has been awarded to Project Manager, Chief Technical Advisor, Hydrographic Position, Gender/Gender-based Violence Specialist, Community Liaison Officer, Monitoring and Evaluation Specialist, Administrative Officer, Social Safeguards Specialist, and Environment Safeguards Specialist. A contract was also signed with a Mentoring Firm to mentor MISE staff who will oversee rehabilitation of project causeways and support MICT with supervision of maritime works executed under the Design-Build contract. Hydrographical survey services had commenced in February 2023 and is nearing completion. The updated nautical charts for the four outer islands are expected to be produced by December 2024.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Audited Project Financial Statements | Jun 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/53043/53043-001-apfs-en_1.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Environmental and Social Monitoring Reports | Oct 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/53043/53043-001-esmr-en_5.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Most of the data collection was completed within one year from the start of survey work on 7 February 2023. All vessel-based Multi-Beam Echo Sounder (MBES) data collection is completed but about 10% of Lidar data for Tabiteuea is still being gathered and will be sent to the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) by September 2024. The bathymetric survey data for Abaiang, Beru, Nonouti and Tabiteuea will be provided to the Mentoring Firm and Design-Build contractor by September 2024, which will enable designs for key civil works activities to be prepared. UKHO will review the data and produce the updated nautical charts for the four KOITIIP outer islands by 31 December 2024. The complex, high-value design-build contract is for signing, with the aid of an international engineering consultant. OIIU anticipates successfully awarding and signing the contract by end-September 2024. Installation of AtoNs is expected to commence in mid-2025. OIIU will undertake further consultations with women on project islands to define the scope of this activity. The GBV Action Framework outlines mitigation and response measures for GBV and sexual exploitation, abuse, and harassment (SEAH). A dedicated phone line and email address have been established to report any GBV issues associated with KOITIIP, and awareness raising signs will be set up at work sites. Training in the GBV Action Framework, inductions to the Code of Conduct, and refreshers are being undertaken for the implementing entities and consultants engaged in the project. 20 staff (18 men and 2 women) from IIC (hydrographic surveys) received training on the GBV Framework and Kiribati&apos;s penal code, and signed codes of conduct before mobilizing to the field. Two training programs on gender sensitivity and GBV requirements under KOITIIP were held and attended by 20 (Abaiang) and 12 (Tarawa) participants respectively, half of which were men. Consultations and training on KOITIIP&apos;s GBV Framework were also carried out on KOITIIP&apos;s four outer islands. The four events were attended by 130 men and 178 women (collectively). A Mentoring Firm has been selected and signed, and mobilization of staff to Kiribati has commenced in June 2024.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
